Now the ClearanceValidator service. Design:

```java
@Component
public class SectionClearanceValidator {
    // validateCandidate(plan, occupancies, configs, excludePlanIds) → List<Map<String,Object>> conflicts (422 details)
    // validatePublishedSet(sectionId, config) → void, throws 409
}
```

Internal slot representation for merged checking: need scheduleKey, trainNo, direction, start, end. Both Occupancy (candidate) and PublishedSlot can be adapted. I'll make a private record SlotView.

validateCandidate:
```java
public List<Map<String, Object>> validateCandidate(DayPlan plan, List<Occupancy> occupancies,
                                                   Map<String, SectionConfig> configs,
                                                   List<Long> excludePlanIds) {
    List<Map<String, Object>> conflicts = new ArrayList<>();
    // group candidate occupancies by configured section
    Map<String, List<Occupancy>> bySection = new LinkedHashMap<>();
    for (Occupancy o : occupancies) {
        if (configs.containsKey(o.sectionId())) {
            bySection.computeIfAbsent(o.sectionId(), k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(o);
        }
    }
    if (bySection.isEmpty()) return conflicts;
    // direction pre-check for candidates
    for (var e : bySection.entrySet()) {
        SectionConfig config = configs.get(e.getKey());
        for (Occupancy o : e.getValue()) {
            if (o.direction() == null || o.direction().isBlank()) {
                conflicts.add(detail "DIRECTION_REQUIRED" ...);
            } else if (!config.allows(o.direction())) {
                conflicts.add(detail "DIRECTION_UNKNOWN" ... allowedForward/allowedBackward);
            }
        }
    }
    if (!conflicts.isEmpty()) return conflicts; // 方向非法时不继续间隔检查
    // published slots for these sections
    List<PublishedSlot> published = planRepo.findPublishedSlots(plan.opDate(), bySection.keySet(), excludePlanIds);
    // 已发布无方向占用不能猜方向
    for (PublishedSlot s : published) {
        if (configs.containsKey(s.sectionId()) && (s.direction() == null || s.direction().isBlank())) {
            throw conflict 409 OCCUPANCY_DIRECTION_UNKNOWN
        }
    }
    // merge per section and check adjacent pairs
    for (var e : bySection.entrySet()) {
        String sectionId = e.getKey();
        SectionConfig config = configs.get(sectionId);
        List<SlotView> merged = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Occupancy o : e.getValue()) merged.add(new SlotView(plan.scheduleKey(), o.trainNo(), o.direction(), o.startUtc(), o.endUtc()));
        for (PublishedSlot s : published) if (s.sectionId().equals(sectionId)) merged.add(...);
        merged.sort(comparator);
        conflicts.addAll(checkAdjacentPairs(sectionId, config.clearanceSeconds(), merged));
    }
    return conflicts;
}
```

checkAdjacentPairs:
```java
private List<Map<String,Object>> checkAdjacentPairs(String sectionId, int clearanceSeconds, List<SlotView> sorted) {
    List<Map<String,Object>> conflicts = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int i = 1; i < sorted.size(); i++) {
        SlotView prev = sorted.get(i-1);
        SlotView cur = sorted.get(i);
        if (cur.startUtc().isBefore(prev.endUtc())) {
            conflicts.add(sectionConflict detail);
        } else if (!prev.direction().equals(cur.direction())) {
            long gap = Duration.between(prev.endUtc(), cur.startUtc()).getSeconds();
            if (gap < clearanceSeconds) {
                conflicts.add(clearance detail with actualGapSeconds, requiredClearanceSeconds);
            }
        }
    }
    return conflicts;
}
```

